Name:                   hledger-interest
Version:                2.0.0
Synopsis:               computes interest for a given account
License:                BSD3
License-file:           LICENSE
Author:                 Peter Simons <simons@cryp.to>
Maintainer:             Peter Simons <simons@cryp.to>
Homepage:               https://github.com/peti/hledger-interest
Category:               Finance
Build-type:             Simple
Cabal-version:          2.0
Extra-source-files:     README.md
Extra-doc-files:        CHANGELOG.md
                        tests/fixtures/*.journal
                        tests/fixtures/*.rates
                        tests/golden/*.golden
Stability:              stable
tested-with:            GHC == 9.6.7, GHC == 9.8.4, GHC == 9.10.3,
                        GHC == 9.12.2, GHC == 9.14.1

Description:
 hledger-interest is a small command-line utility based on Simon
 Michael's hledger library. Its purpose is to compute interest for a
 given ledger account. Using command line flags, the program can be
 configured to use various schemes for day-counting, such as act\/act,
 30\/360, 30E\/360, and 30E\/360isda. It supports constant rates,
 annual interest with a fixed rate, and schedules of annual rates
 supplied on the command line or read from a text file.
 .
 As an example, consider the loan in the regression fixture
 @tests/fixtures/boundaries.journal@:
 .
 > 2023-01-31 Loan
 >     Assets:Bank          EUR 10000.00
 >     Liabilities:Loan
 >
 > 2023-02-28 Payment
 >     Assets:Bank          EUR -100.00
 >     Liabilities:Loan
 >
 > 2023-03-31 Payment
 >     Assets:Bank          EUR -100.00
 >     Liabilities:Loan
 >
 > 2023-07-01 Payment on rate change
 >     Assets:Bank          EUR -100.00
 >     Liabilities:Loan
 >
 > 2023-07-01 Second payment on same day
 >     Assets:Bank          EUR -50.00
 >     Liabilities:Loan
 >
 > 2024-01-15 Payment after year end
 >     Assets:Bank          EUR -100.00
 >     Liabilities:Loan
 >
 > 2024-02-29 Leap day payment
 >     Assets:Bank          EUR -100.00
 >     Liabilities:Loan
 >
 > 2024-03-31 Payment
 >     Assets:Bank          EUR -100.00
 >     Liabilities:Loan
 >
 > 2024-04-01 Unrelated transaction
 >     Assets:Bank          EUR -10.00
 >     Expenses:Other
 .
 With 5% annual interest and actual-day counting, crediting interest
 to the loan account compounds it. The following command prints only
 the generated interest postings; its output is checked by the
 @annual-act@ golden test:
 .
 > $ hledger-interest --file=tests/fixtures/boundaries.journal --source=Expenses:Interest --target=Liabilities:Loan --act --annual=0.05 --quiet Liabilities:Loan
 > 2023-02-28 5% interest for EUR -10000.00 over 28 days
 >     Liabilities:Loan       EUR -38.36
 >     Expenses:Interest       EUR 38.36
 >
 > 2023-03-31 5% interest for EUR -9938.36 over 31 days
 >     Liabilities:Loan       EUR -42.20
 >     Expenses:Interest       EUR 42.20
 >
 > 2023-07-01 5% interest for EUR -9880.56 over 92 days
 >     Liabilities:Loan      EUR -124.52
 >     Expenses:Interest      EUR 124.52
 >
 > 2023-12-31 5% interest for EUR -9855.08 over 183 days
 >     Liabilities:Loan      EUR -247.05
 >     Expenses:Interest      EUR 247.05
 >
 > 2024-01-15 5% interest for EUR -10102.13 over 15 days
 >     Liabilities:Loan       EUR -20.70
 >     Expenses:Interest       EUR 20.70
 >
 > 2024-02-29 5% interest for EUR -10022.84 over 45 days
 >     Liabilities:Loan       EUR -61.62
 >     Expenses:Interest       EUR 61.62
 >
 > 2024-03-31 5% interest for EUR -9984.45 over 31 days
 >     Liabilities:Loan       EUR -42.28
 >     Expenses:Interest       EUR 42.28
 .
 Running the utility with @--help@ gives a brief overview over the
 available options:
 .
 > Usage: hledger-interest [OPTION...] ACCOUNT
 > Default: post at transactions, rate-period ends, and year ends.
 >   -h          --help                      print this message and exit
 >   -V          --version                   show version number and exit
 >   -v          --verbose                   print matching input transactions and generated interest (default)
 >   -q          --quiet                     print generated interest only
 >               --today                     alias for --until=today
 >               --until=DATE                compute interest through DATE (YYYY-MM-DD or today);
 >                                           exclude transactions with later effective dates
 >               --post-on-transactions      post only at transactions (and at --until/--today);
 >                                           skip rate-period and automatic year-end postings;
 >                                           overrides --post-on-rate-changes
 >               --post-on-rate-changes      post at transactions and rate-period ends;
 >                                           skip automatic year-end postings;
 >                                           --post-on-transactions takes precedence;
 >                                           --until/--today also post on the final day
 >   -f FILE     --file=FILE                 input ledger file (pass '-' for stdin)
 >                                           default: $LEDGER_FILE or ~/.hledger.journal
 >   -s ACCOUNT  --source=ACCOUNT            interest source account
 >   -t ACCOUNT  --target=ACCOUNT            interest target account
 >   -I          --ignore-assertions         ignore any failing balance assertions
 >               --act                       use 'act/act' day counting convention
 >                                           (Actual/Actual ISDA; see README)
 >               --30-360                    use '30/360' day counting convention
 >               --30E-360                   use '30E/360' day counting convention
 >               --30E-360isda               use '30E/360isda' day counting convention
 >               --constant=RATE             fixed annual interest rate
 >               --annual=RATE               alias for --constant
 >               --schedule=SCHEDULE         annualized rates and their effective dates;
 >                                           rates are fractions: 0.05 means 5% per year
 >                                           syntax: '[(Date1,Rate1),(Date2,Rate2),...]'
 >               --schedule-file=PATH        read a schedule from a text file;
 >                                           one date and rate per line, starting in column 1;
 >                                           rates: 0.05 or 5%; hledger comments allowed
 >               --annual-schedule=SCHEDULE  alias for --schedule

Source-Repository head
  Type:                 git
  Location:             https://github.com/peti/hledger-interest.git

Executable hledger-interest
  default-language:     Haskell2010
  hs-source-dirs:       src
  Main-is:              hledger-interest.hs
  Build-depends:        base >= 4.9 && < 5, hledger-lib >= 1.32 && < 1.53, time, mtl, Decimal, text, megaparsec >= 7
  other-modules:        Hledger.Interest
                        Hledger.Interest.DayCountConvention
                        Hledger.Interest.Rate
                        Hledger.Interest.ScheduleFile
                        Paths_hledger_interest
  autogen-modules:      Paths_hledger_interest

Test-suite regression
  type:                exitcode-stdio-1.0
  default-language:    Haskell2010
  hs-source-dirs:      tests
  main-is:             golden-tests.hs
  other-modules:       HistoricalRates
  build-depends:       base >= 4.9 && < 5, bytestring, typed-process, Decimal, time, tasty,
                       tasty-golden >= 2.3.6, tasty-hunit
  build-tool-depends:  hledger-interest:hledger-interest

Test-suite calculations
  type:                exitcode-stdio-1.0
  default-language:    Haskell2010
  hs-source-dirs:      tests src
  main-is:             calculation-tests.hs
  other-modules:       Hledger.Interest
                       Hledger.Interest.DayCountConvention
                       Hledger.Interest.Rate
  build-depends:       base >= 4.9 && < 5, hledger-lib >= 1.32 && < 1.53,
                       time, mtl, Decimal, text, tasty, tasty-hunit
